                'en' => 'The express locomotive crushed the rear van and three coaches of the suburban train, then derailed to the left; its tender, thrown onto the wreckage, crushed the leading van and two more coaches. The debris brought down a wall, tore off the station canopy and the telegraph wires and damaged the footbridge. Train no. 214, damaged, was able to continue to Paris.',
