                'en' => 'A signalman opened a semaphore that had been closed to protect the suburban train, letting the express onto an occupied track; the company management spoke of a "moment of aberration" caused by routine. The inquiry found that three of the six staff planned for the station were absent, on the last Sunday of the Exposition Universelle, that the signalman had been called away to deal with train no. 214, which was crowded, late and strengthened with two extra coaches, and that he misread a disc signal.',
